 Norton, Eleanor Holmes [D-DC-At Large]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"DC"},{"bioguideId":"T000468","fullName":"Rep. Titus, Dina [D-NV-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-06","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NV"},{"bioguideId":"G000607","fullName":"Rep. Gallagher, James [R-CA-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"J000288","fullName":"Rep. Johnson, Henry C. \"Hank\" [D-GA-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"GA"},{"bioguideId":"C001072","fullName":"Rep. Carson, André [D-IN-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"},{"bioguideId":"W000808","fullName":"Rep. Wilson, Frederica S. [D-FL-24]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"B001315","fullName":"Rep. Budzinski, Nikki [D-IL-13]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-21","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IL"},{"bioguideId":"C001080","fullName":"Rep. Chu, Judy [D-CA-28]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-08-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"F000477","fullName":"Rep. Foushee, Valerie P. [D-NC-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-08-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"T000487","fullName":"Rep. Tokuda, Jill N. [D-HI-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-08-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"HI"},{"bioguideId":"W000829","fullName":"Rep. Wied, Tony [R-WI-8]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-01","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WI"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T22:15:48+00:00","id":"hr4669-119","introducedDate":"2025-07-23","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-09-03","text":"Ordered to be Reported (Amended) by the Yeas and Nays: 57 - 3."},"laws":[],"number":"4669","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Emergency Management","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"G000546","district":6,"fullName":"Rep. Graves, Sam [R-MO-6]","party":"R","state":"MO"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-07-23","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Fixing Emergency Management for Americans Act of 2025 or the FEMA Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill reestablishes the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) (currently within the Department of Homeland Security) as an independent, cabinet-level agency. It also makes broad changes to&nbsp;FEMA’s disaster and hazard mitigation assistance programs.</p><p>The bill generally transfers&nbsp;FEMA’s current functions and authorities to the independent FEMA, except for certain security-related programs.&nbsp;</p><p>The bill makes various changes to the Public Assistance program, including by</p><ul><li>establishing new grants for expedited funding to repair or replace disaster-damaged facilities,</li><li>establishing block grants that recipients may choose instead of Public Assistance for smaller disasters,</li><li>expediting and expanding uses of funding for emergency response and debris removal, and</li><li>allowing use of excess administrative funds for increasing recipients’ disaster management capacity.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>The bill makes various changes to the Individual Assistance program, including by</p><ul><li>expanding eligibility for housing assistance,</li><li>expanding mitigation and direct (non-financial) assistance for residences,</li><li>reducing certain restrictions on funds duplicating program benefits, and&nbsp;</li><li>establishing a unified disaster application system.</li></ul><p>The bill makes various changes to&nbsp;FEMA’s mitigation programs, including by</p><ul><li>establishing mitigation plans with preapproved projects,</li><li>authorizing an entire Hazard Mitigation Grant Program grant to be provided before costs are incurred,</li><li>changing pre-disaster mitigation assistance to noncompetitive formula grants, and&nbsp;</li><li>allowing recipients to combine mitigation project funds from multiple federal programs.</li></ul><p>Additionally, federal entities must publish various information relating to disaster assistance and conduct various studies on related topics (e.g., preliminary damage assessments, fast-moving disasters, and government emergency alerting systems).&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2026-05-01T14:20:26Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"FEMA Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-02T08:06:36Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-02T08:06:36Z"}
